course: dictionary
lesson: 13107
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can do more than one job. Flaps is one of them. As a verb it is an action word: «The bird flaps its wings.» Here flaps tells you what the bird is doing, moving its wings up and down.
explain: Flaps can also be a noun in its plural form. Plural means more than one. A flap is a flat piece fixed on one side that covers an opening, so «The cat door has two flaps» means there are two flat pieces covering openings.
explain: How do you tell which job it does? Look at the sentence. If someone or something is doing an action, flaps is a verb. If you could count it, as in two or three, it is a noun. Try swapping in another action word: «The bird waves its wings» still makes sense, so flaps is a verb there.
fact: Flaps is a verb when something does the action, as in «The bird flaps its wings.»
fact: Flaps is a noun when it means more than one flap, as in «The envelope has two flaps.»
fact: A flap can be a flat piece that covers an opening, such as a pocket flap or a cat flap.
fact: On an aeroplane, the wing has movable parts called flaps. The aeroplane lowers its flaps to slow down and land.
fact: In a lift-the-flap book, you lift a flap to find a hidden picture.
exercise: «The bird flaps its wings and rises into the sky.» What job does flaps do in this sentence? | An adjective, describing a thing | A noun, a thing | A name for a place | *A verb, an action
exercise: «The envelope has two flaps that you must open carefully.» Is flaps a verb or a noun here? | *A noun, more than one flat piece | A question word | A verb, something being done | A colour
exercise: Which sentence uses flaps as a plural noun? | She flaps her book shut | The wind flaps the washing on the line | The owl flaps silently over the lake | *The cat door has two flaps for it to pass through
test: In «The aeroplane lowers its flaps to slow down», what is flaps? | *A noun, movable parts on the wing | A verb, an action | A question word | A name for a person
test: Which phrase uses flaps as a verb? | *the bird flaps its wings | two pocket flaps | a lift-the-flap page | the flaps of the tent
exam: Which word is the plural noun in «The wind flaps the tent flaps all night»? | *the second flaps | the first flaps | wind | night
